    "note": "Parliamentary republic under the 1994 Constitution. On 1 January 2000 the President (Petru Lucinschi) was directly elected; the 2000 constitutional revision made the President elected by Parliament with a three-fifths (61-vote) majority, first applied in 2001. Repeated failures to reach 61 votes led to early elections (2001, July 2009, 2010) and acting presidents from September 2009 to March 2012. A 2010 referendum to restore direct election failed for low turnout; on 4 March 2016 the Constitutional Court ruled the 2000 revision unconstitutional, and direct two-round elections resumed in 2016. Transnistria (PMR) has been outside the government's control since the early 1990s."
  },
